{
 "HOW_IT_WAS_ANSWERED": "The per-event pieces survive in the same artifact (weights_push, mc_indices), so the recorded scalars were DECOMPOSED per cell using the producer's own definition (train_fullevent_nominal.py:576-577): ratio[c] = sum_c(w_reco*push)/sum_c(w_reco), the w_reco-weighted mean push in cell c. A pure scale deficit makes that constant.",
 "NOISE": "Per-cell sampling error of the weighted mean was computed from the within-cell weighted variance of push, and the OBSERVED dispersion compared against the dispersion expected from that alone. This is not a marginal call: the observed sd is 68.4x the noise-expected sd on the truth grid and 36.3x on the reco grid. BEN-025 warns against letting a small-sample spread settle a question; this spread is two orders of magnitude clear of that concern.",
 "STRUCTURE": "The variation is dominated by p_parallel, not pT. Truth grid: the p_parallel marginal runs 0.272 -> 1.321, a factor of 4.9, and is smooth and monotone over most of its range; the pT marginal spans only 0.646 -> 0.944. The reco grid reproduces both. It is NOT an artefact of the dead-cell staircase -- those cells sit ABOVE the global mean (0.833 vs 0.717), so excluding them would not rescue the argument.",
 "THE_ARGUMENT_TESTED": "VL100 = 0.512603276 is computed on UNIT-NORMALIZED 285-cell spectra, and the quotability case is that an overall normalization deficit divides out under that normalization. That holds if and only if the deficit is scale-only.",
 "THE_CONTROL_THAT_MATTERED": "The trainer uses the LOADER's mc.weight_reco (:564-565), not the NPZ's raw w_reco, so the absolute sums differ by 31.6% and the first version of this probe correctly REFUSED to report. What the per-cell ratios need is only that the two weights differ by a GLOBAL SCALE. Tested rather than assumed: k was fixed from the DENOMINATOR alone (1.462888717614880) and the NUMERATOR then reproduced to a residual of 2.0e-13. That is a real test -- the numerator weights each event by push and the denominator does not, so any per-event discrepancy would have broken one and not the other.",
 "VERDICT": "SHAPE-DEPENDENT. NOT scale-only. The premise the VL100 quotability ruling rests on is FALSE.",
 "WHAT_THIS_DOES_NOT_SAY": [
  "It does not say VL100 is wrong. It says the specific argument offered for quoting it -- that the deficit divides out under unit normalization -- does not hold, because the deficit is not an overall factor.",
  "It does not quantify how much VL100 itself moves. That would need the recovery recomputed under a shape-corrected fold-forward, which is a separate calculation and was not run.",
  "It says nothing about the other three quotability grounds, which are hygiene rather than physics and were not examined here."
 ],
 "WHY_THE_RECORDED_FIELD_COULD_NOT_ANSWER_IT": "pet_diagnostic_quarantine.measured_fold_forward_dev reads two SCALARS -- fold_forward_sum_w_push_reco and fold_forward_sum_w_reco -- and forms dev = |(num/den)/R - 1|. Both are sums over the entire reco leg, so the shape information is integrated away BEFORE the number exists. The recorded quantity is definitionally incapable of distinguishing scale from shape, at any precision.",
 "measured_utc_date": "2026-08-14",
 "n_pass_reco": 837671,
 "n_subsample": 2000000,
